# Headless (no graphics yet): needs the compositor, so it does not run. It is one of the four
# snapshot-boot components (with tvservice, WebAppMgr and inputcommon; the last two are not
# started headless either), and the first of them to be ready emits snapshot-component-ready,
# on which snapshot-boot-sync emits snapshot-resume-done and mount-readwrite runs. LG's tvservice
# waits for mount-readwrite's flag before it announces itself (libsnapshot-boot's
# snapshot_boot_ready), so without a graphical component nothing would. Stand in for this one,
# on the stock `start on lsm-ready`. The stock `stop on` includes `stopping surface-manager`,
# which headless (a one-shot job that only emits lsm-ready) does at once: that stopped this task
# before it had emitted.
stop on starting start_update
task
script
	initctl emit --no-wait snapshot-component-ready SNAPSHOT_COMPONENT=mvpdwin
end script
